 PEDIATRICS:The American Academy of Pediatrics is a professional association of pediatricians dedicated to the health and well-being of infants, children, adolescents, and young adults.", "TEST DE TOLERANCIA ORAL A LA GLUCOSA:El Test de Tolerancia Oral a la Glucosa (TTOG) es un procedimiento diagnóstico utilizado para detectar alteraciones en el metabolismo de los carbohidratos, que implica la administración de una bebida con glucosa y la medición de los niveles de glucemia en diferentes intervalos de tiempo.", "GASTRECTOMÍAS:Las gastrectomías son procedimientos quirúrgicos que implican la extirpación parcial o total del estómago, lo que puede afectar la interpretación de pruebas como el TTOG.", "NATIONAL DIABETES DATA GROUP:The National Diabetes Data Group (NDDG) is an organization dedicated to providing guidelines and standards for the diagnosis and management of diabetes, including gestational diabetes. It has established criteria for the classification and diagnosis of diabetes mellitus and other categories of glucose intolerance, ensuring a comprehensive approach to understanding and addressing diabetes-related health issues.", "TTOG:The TTOG (test de tolerancia oral a la glucosa) is a medical test used to diagnose diabetes by measuring blood glucose levels after the ingestion of glucose.", "O'SULLIVAN TEST:The O'Sullivan test is a screening test for gestational diabetes that involves measuring blood glucose levels after consuming a glucose solution.", "GLUCÓMETRO:A glucómetro is a device used for measuring blood glucose levels, particularly in patients with diabetes.", "ANÁLISIS QUÍMICO DE VAN DE KAMER:The análisis químico de Van de Kamer is a reference method used for the quantitative determination of fat in fecal samples, important for diagnosing conditions like esteatorrea.", "ACIDO ASCORBICO:A substance that can interfere with medical tests and is commonly known as Vitamin C.", "TOCOFEROL:TOCOFEROL is a substance commonly known as Vitamin E, which can interfere with medical tests. It is a form of vitamin E that is utilized as an antioxidant in dietary supplements.", "ADITIVOS ANTIOXIDANTES:Antioxidant additives that should be removed from the diet prior to certain medical tests to avoid false negatives."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}